diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b4fa3bd8665c3011050388ff76688076e8f6b6cc..fac568cd7c3d1349c7d1850416d89a7c9d0179ae 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -18,3 +18,11 @@ first. A refused code leaves the order as it was.
 The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before the discount, so a
 discount cannot lose an order its free shipping. An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents`, and
 `totalCents` is the items, less the discount, plus the shipping.
+
+## Monthly export
+
+`exportMonth(month)` gives the accountant the orders placed in a month, as CSV text for her spreadsheet. The month is
+`YYYY-MM`; the text has a header line `order,date,customer,total` and then one line per order, by order number.
+`date` is the date the order stores, and `total` is what the customer pays in euros (`12.50`), so it already includes
+the discount and the shipping. The export leaves out the customers' email addresses and phone numbers. A month with no orders gives the header line alone, and a month that is not
+`YYYY-MM` is refused. Lines end in CRLF, as RFC 4180 has them; a value with a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted.
